-- FINDING 5.  The language has no publication-time axis, and a rule-effective date can be earlier than the day
-- the text became known.
--  (a) A retrospective version given its deemed commencement (1 Jan 2011) as its rule-effective date is applied
--      to a reader of 1 Aug 2012, who could not have known of it (silent).  Printed: line (a) gives FALSE; the
--      reader of 1 Aug 2012 is told a television set was not scheduled for conduct in June 2011.
--  (b) The fix is a SECOND date in the rule, compared with TODAY.  Printed: line (b) gives TRUE for the
--      reader of 1 Aug 2012 and FALSE for the reader of 1 Nov 2012.
--  (c) `RULES ENCODED DATE` is not an identifier: the encoded-time axis has a writer (`EVAL UNDER RULES ENCODED
--      AT`) and no reader, and it is about when the L4 was drafted, not when the law was published (f05b).
IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate
TIMEZONE IS "Asia/Singapore"

`TV scheduled, no publication gate` MEANS
    IF `RULES EFFECTIVE DATE` AT LEAST (Date 1 1 2011) THEN FALSE ELSE TRUE

`TV scheduled, with publication gate` MEANS
    IF `RULES EFFECTIVE DATE` AT LEAST (Date 1 1 2011) AND TODAY AT LEAST (Date 31 10 2012) THEN FALSE ELSE TRUE

-- (a)
#EVAL `EVAL AS OF SYSTEM TIME` (Date 1 8 2012) (`EVAL UNDER VALID TIME` (Date 1 6 2011) `TV scheduled, no publication gate`)
-- (b)
#EVAL `EVAL AS OF SYSTEM TIME` (Date 1 8 2012) (`EVAL UNDER VALID TIME` (Date 1 6 2011) `TV scheduled, with publication gate`)
#EVAL `EVAL AS OF SYSTEM TIME` (Date 1 11 2012) (`EVAL UNDER VALID TIME` (Date 1 6 2011) `TV scheduled, with publication gate`)
